;;; A hypothesis rule whose conclusion is an `and` inside an `and` proposed one
;;; fact headed `and`, a commitment no state can hold.
;;;
;;; A nested `(and …)` in a hypothesis: the inner one was a template headed `and`,
;;; and as the first conjunct it was the one the hypothesis layer read
;;; (`hrule-and.ein`), so H was `{(and (p a) (q a))}`, one candidate over the
;;; relation `and`, and R two states, the second holding `(and (p a) (q a))`;
;;; `(r a)` was proposed by nothing. The right answer is `hrule-and.ein`'s, a
;;; refusal (Q-M1f.271): written under `open`, the conjunction is refused at the
;;; parse, `and` heading no fact (Q-M1f.567).
;;;
(relation p Thing :why "p {?3}")
(relation q Thing :why "q {?3}")
(relation r Thing :why "r {?3}")
(rule h () :match () :assert (open (and (and (p a) (q a)) (r a))) :why "propose p and q, and r, of a")
